25,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The earth-moving firms are worried about clay and slippage. Big digs look risky, but small work is fine.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"People mostly stick to the firm ground to reach the tram. Also, the drainage is struggling and it gets very hot.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Minato,,"We have very few staff left, but we have volunteers for habitat work and sports.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The water basin from years ago is still great, but the paved areas are falling apart quickly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The habitat fund covers planting and water, but not buildings. Also, planted areas are much more expensive to maintain.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if people want firm ground, maybe we shouldn't do too many paths?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, I think they just want the most direct route. @Minako, that's interesting about the basin.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, if the fund pays for planting, maybe that helps the cost?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, only for the start. @Jonathan mentioned the upkeep is the real problem.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,Exactly. The long-term budget is the primary concern for the city.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, if the basin is still good, maybe a water-based plan is safer?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, would a paved plaza be cheaper to maintain than a forest or wetland?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, but we have volunteers for the other things, not for cleaning a plaza.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I agree with Kenji. The water works lasted, while the paving failed.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Paving is cheaper per hectare, but the habitat fund makes the initial cost of wetlands easier.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried about the clay, though. A huge pond might be a nightmare to dig.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,We need to balance the heat and drainage issues with the actual usage patterns.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Minato,,I just want to make sure whoever is in charge isn't overwhelmed.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Minako,,The evidence suggests that nature-based solutions have lasted longer here.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,We must consider the funding terms and the maintenance gap.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
